# Compat lane PR-3 + corrective lanes S1/S2: the flag-gated shadow analysis wiring (VERIPSA_COMPAT_ANALYSIS +
# VERIPSA_COMPAT_REPOS, default OFF everywhere) under the CORRECTED baseline-anchored semantics
# (docs/COMPATIBILITY_TRAFFIC_CONTROL_PLAN.md). Candidate pairs from the impact surface + main-graph adjacency
# + a transient import scan (cross-file pairs, cap/budget-disciplined), with exact source provenance and
# explicit candidacy completeness (read/parser/head/cap failure is never a silent empty set); each PR's OWN target-branch merge-base
# is the baseline shape point; 4-way per-contract classification with delta-derived roles + canonical symmetric
# fingerprints (py-call-v1); reason vocabulary v2 (contract_delta:<rule> / rebase_needed /
# divergent_definitions — breaking:*/risky:* retired) plus the S2 evidence-gated class
# consumer_call_mismatch:<detail> (positional_shortfall / missing_required_kwonly / callee_removed), recorded
# ONLY when the counterpart PR's own changed files contain a call of the changed/removed contract that is
# provably incompatible with the NEW shape. Shadow-OFF must stay byte-identical to pre-PR behavior; shadow-ON
# must change no output; the PR-4 solver consumes ONLY the evidence-backed consumer_call_mismatch rows.
register_gate "tests/test_compat_shadow_analysis.py" "COMPAT SHADOW ANALYSIS GATE: PASS" "compat shadow analysis wiring: flag-gated baseline-anchored 4-way classification + evidence-gated consumer mismatch + symmetric shadow persistence" "compat shadow analysis (compatibility lanes PR-3/PR-4 + corrective lanes S1/S2): behind VERIPSA_COMPAT_ANALYSIS + the VERIPSA_COMPAT_REPOS CSV allowlist (both default OFF; either off = the module returns before ANY work), the webhook brain pairs the acting PR with up to VERIPSA_COMPAT_PAIR_CAP candidate sibling open PRs from THREE deduped candidacy sources — a shared changed .py path on the ALREADY-computed impact surface (no new DB queries), main-graph 1-hop adjacency read from the surface's per-change blast radius, and a transient in-memory import scan over the changed .py files for NEW files the main graph cannot see. Provenance is split as pairs_via_main_graph vs pairs_via_import_scan (pairs_via_graph remains a legacy aggregate); head/read/parser/cap uncertainty reports candidacy_complete=false with bounded unknown/capped metadata, never a silent empty candidate set. EACH PR's baseline is its merge-base with the target branch; four shape points and Consumer Expectations produce consumer_call_mismatch:<detail> only for proven breakage. Main-graph candidacy is proven end-to-end through the REAL ingest_graph_with_authority and main_impact_surface from BOTH event orders; the canonical NEW-file fixture separately proves import fallback. Shadow-OFF remains byte-identical; all persistence/logging is content-free counts/metadata only." "compat shadow analysis S1+S2: flags-OFF byte identity + zero work; real persisted graph and new-file import fallback have separate provenance; failed/capped candidacy is explicitly incomplete; baseline-anchored roles and canonical fingerprints converge from both event orders; evidence-backed mismatch rules only; caps/parser/read failures never become compatible; sentinels nowhere in DB or logs. Gate 247." 24 420
